drm_ctx: never take a status panel (panel-mipi-dbi) for the game display

gfx_ctx_drm_init() lists /dev/dri in readdir order and takes the first card
with a connected connector. On the Pi 4 arcade case the small SPI status LCD
(panel-mipi-dbi, card2) is such a card, and it was listed before vc4 (card0):
every game opened on the 320x240 panel and exited with

  [ERROR] [KMS/EGL]: Did not find suitable video mode for 1920 x 1080.
  [ERROR] [Video]: Cannot open video driver.. Exiting..

Skip devices whose DRM driver is panel-mipi-dbi; the launcher does the same.

--- a/gfx/drivers_context/drm_ctx.c	2026-10-22 20:40:43.036657774 +0300
+++ b/gfx/drivers_context/drm_ctx.c	2026-10-22 20:40:43.056657793 +0300
@@ -746,6 +746,23 @@
 
    fd = drm->fd;
 
+   /* An SPI status panel (panel-mipi-dbi, the Pi 4 arcade case's LCD) is a
+    * KMS device with a connected connector too, and /dev/dri is listed in
+    * readdir order, so it can come first. Games belong on the main display:
+    * never take the panel. */
+   {
+      drmVersionPtr ver = drmGetVersion(fd);
+      bool info_panel   = ver && ver->name
+         && string_is_equal(ver->name, "panel-mipi-dbi");
+      if (ver)
+         drmFreeVersion(ver);
+      if (info_panel)
+      {
+         RARCH_LOG("[KMS]: Skipping %s (status panel).\n", gpu);
+         goto nextgpu;
+      }
+   }
+
    if (!drm_get_resources(fd))
       goto nextgpu;
 
